-- title:
--   Value group over ℚ is divisible-hull generated by v(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure such that $K$ is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $A \subseteq K$ be a valuation subring, with $A.valuation$ the associated multiplicative valuation $v \colon K \to \Gamma_A \cup \{0\}$ on the value group of $A$ (written multiplicatively, so that $v(y) \le 1$ exactly when $y \in A$). Let $p$ be a prime number whose image in $K$ satisfies $v(p) < 1$, i.e. $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$. Then for every $x \in K$ with $x \neq 0$ there exist a natural number $n$ with $0 < n$ and an integer $k$ such that $v(x)^n = v(p)^k$ in $\Gamma_A \cup \{0\}$, the right-hand side being an integer power in the group of units. In additive notation: the value group of $A$ is contained in the divisible hull of the cyclic subgroup generated by $v(p)$, so that $x \mapsto k/n$ is a $\mathbb{Q}$-valued order function on $K^\times$ normalised by the value at $p$.
--
--   This is the standard fact that a valuation on an algebraic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ lying above $p$ has value group torsion over the value group $p^{\mathbb{Z}}$ of the $p$-adic valuation, hence is of rank one and real-valued after embedding into $\mathbb{R}_{>0}$. It is used in the construction of ring homomorphisms from valuation subrings into $p$-adic completions and in the analysis of prolongations of places along models of modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_pow_valuation_eq_valuation_natCast_zpow_of_isAlgebraic.lean

